%I A400651 #5 Oct 07 2026 23:15:30
%S A400651 28,57,119,146,122,78,18,2
%N A400651 Number of n-uniform honeycombs of Euclidean 3-space by convex uniform polyhedra having n different vertex stars.
%C A400651 The three-dimensional analog of A068600. A honeycomb here is a face-to-face tiling of Euclidean 3-space by convex uniform polyhedra with unit edges (Platonic and Archimedean solids, prisms and antiprisms). It is counted by a(n) when its vertices fall into exactly n orbits under its symmetry group and the n orbits carry n pairwise distinct vertex stars (arrangements of cells around a vertex), which is Krötenheerdt's condition for tilings of the plane. Honeycombs are counted up to congruence.
%C A400651 The sequence is finite: a(n) = 0 for n >= 9, one index later than A068600, which vanishes for n >= 8.
%C A400651 a(1) = 28 = A242941(3) is the number of convex uniform honeycombs.
%C A400651 a(n) >= A068600(n) for all n, since the prismatic lift of a planar tiling counted by A068600(n) is a honeycomb counted by a(n).
%C A400651 For n >= 2, a(n) = A068600(n) + V(n) + H(n) + W(n), where V counts stackings of slabs of tetrahedra, octahedra and triangular prisms (16, 24, 16 for n = 2..4), H counts honeycombs containing truncated tetrahedra (3, 6, 4 for n = 2..4), both zero for n >= 5, and W counts the stackings of layers of cubes and of triangular and hexagonal prisms with prism axes in two perpendicular directions (18, 50, 93, 107, 68, 11, 2 for n = 2..8).
%D A400651 Michel Deza and Mikhail Shtogrin, Uniform partitions of 3-space, their relatives and embedding, European J. Combin. 21 (2000), 807-814.
%H A400651 Mario Càllisto, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23097245">The three-dimensional Krötenheerdt sequence and its vanishing point</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400651 Mario Càllisto, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23096848">krotenheerdt-sequence: machine-checked companion</a>, Zenodo, 2026 (software, with the certificates of the enumeration).
%H A400651 Mario Càllisto, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22881686">The 28 convex uniform honeycombs: a completeness theorem</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%e A400651 a(2) = 57. One of the 57 is no. 13' of Andreini's 1905 list, a honeycomb of tetrahedra and truncated tetrahedra with two vertex stars.
%e A400651 a(8) = 2: two stackings of cube layers and rows of triangular and hexagonal prisms, with eight vertex orbits and eight distinct vertex stars.
%Y A400651 Cf. A068600 (the planar case), A068599, A242941.
%K A400651 nonn,fini,full,new
%O A400651 1,1
